== Corporate affairs ==

=== Ownership ===

RapidAir is a subsidiary of [[Grup RapidAir]], a holding company publicly traded on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker symbol RAP. Grup RapidAir was established as the airline's parent company at the time of the 1998 initial public offering, restructuring the airline's corporate structure to separate the operating airline from its property and financing holdings. The ownership structure of Grup RapidAir is as follows:

* '''Mas family''': 12% — descendants of founder Jordi Mas i Vidal; represented on the board
* '''[[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] (FIDB)''': 7% — acquired at the time of the 1998 listing
* '''[[Balboa Pension Fund]] (BPF)''': 5% — institutional anchor investor
* '''Public float''': approximately 76% — held by institutional and retail investors

=== Leadership ===

Jordi Mas i Vidal served as chief executive from the airline's founding in 1984 until 2005, when he retired and was succeeded by Núria Bosch (b. c. 1970). Bosch had joined the airline in 1998 as operations manager and was appointed chief operating officer in 2002. Her appointment as CEO coincided with the airline's international expansion and the 2013 fleet renewal programme. Mas remained on the board of directors until 2012.

== Services ==

=== Cabin ===

RapidAir operates a single-class {{w|economy class}} cabin on all aircraft. The base fare includes a seat and one personal item that must fit under the seat in front of the passenger. All additional services are charged separately:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Description !! Fee
|-
| Carry-on baggage || One item up to 10 kg, stored in the overhead bin || Charged separately
|-
| Checked baggage || One item up to 20 kg || Charged separately
|-
| Early boarding || Priority boarding group || Charged separately
|-
| Exit row seat || Extra legroom seat at emergency exit row || Charged separately
|-
| First row seat || Extra legroom seat at the front of the cabin || Charged separately
|-
| Seat selection || Standard seat assignment || Charged separately
|}

Seat assignment is not included in the base fare; passengers who do not purchase a seat selection are assigned a seat at check-in. The exit row and first row seats are offered at a premium due to the additional legroom, and are subject to safety regulations governing exit row occupancy.

=== Buy-on-board ===

No complimentary food or beverage service is provided. A buy-on-board programme offers snacks, sandwiches, and beverages for purchase on all flights. Hot meals are available on international services and on domestic flights exceeding 90 minutes.

=== Frequent flyer programme ===

RapidAir does not operate a traditional frequent flyer programme. Instead, the airline offers '''RapidClub''', a subscription programme costing $10 per month, which provides free seat selection and one free checked bag on all bookings. The programme is aimed at frequent domestic travellers on the SCI–SBT and PNU–SBT corridors.

== Accidents and incidents ==

=== 1993 Sant Cristòfor runway incursion ===

On 3 September 1993, a RapidAir Boeing 737-300 was involved in a [[runway incursion]] at [[Sant Cristòfor International Airport]]. The RapidAir aircraft entered Runway 09/27 without clearance while an [[Aeroístmus]] Airbus A310 was on its take-off roll. The A310's crew aborted take-off at approximately 120 knots, stopping approximately 400 metres short of the intersecting RapidAir aircraft. There were no injuries.

The investigation by the [[Balboa Airports Authority]] found that the RapidAir crew had misinterpreted a taxi clearance as a line-up clearance, and that the air traffic controller's phraseology had been ambiguous. The incident prompted the authority to implement mandatory readback procedures for all runway entry clearances and to install enhanced taxiway lighting at SCI.

=== 2008 Portnou ATR 72 runway excursion ===

On 17 November 2008, RapidAir Flight 412, an ATR 72-210 arriving from [[Campdària Airport|Campdària]] at [[Portnou International Airport]], departed the runway during landing in heavy rain. The aircraft veered off the paved surface and came to rest on the grass adjacent to the runway. There were no injuries among the 64 passengers and 4 crew, and the aircraft sustained minor damage to the landing gear.

The investigation attributed the excursion to {{w|hydroplaning}} on the wet runway, combined with a crosswind component that exceeded the crew's corrected approach speed. The incident led RapidAir to revise its wet-runway operating procedures and to increase the minimum visibility requirements for ATR 72 arrivals at airports without {{w|runway grooving}}.

